I don't like the luck system as it stands. My luck, while being
somewhat variable, spends most of the game either at 0 or at 13 (except
on special RL occasions). In other words, during a game I'm either
"normal" or "extremely lucky". I'd like it if luck weren't so binary.

One way to encourage more intermediate luck values would be to have
items which affected your luck while you carried or wielded or wore
them. Something like a rabbit's foot amulet, a cursed cape of calamity,
change a luckstone so it just provides a luck bonus but doesn't affect
prayer timeout (and make them stack!).

I really like the idea of players wondering whether to go for
AC-increasing armor or luck-increasing armor; similarly whether to wear
an amulet of life-saving or a rabbit's foot.

Having said all this, I have never played an atheist game. I imagine
luck is more interesting in one of those!

